docs/extensions.md:8:Both kinds can also give **prompt templates** (`pi.prompts`). See [Prompts](prompts.md#prompt-templates).
docs/extensions.md:69:A [pi-durable](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@earendil-works/pi-durable) extension adds its tools and prompt sections to every conversation: comment mode, `pr_number` runs, and direct prompts. An example is the `pit/durable` extension of [pit](https://github.com/cv/pit):
docs/extensions.md:103:| `agentDir` | `agent_dir`, resolved against the workspace. If `agent_dir` is empty: a new temporary directory in `RUNNER_TEMP` |
docs/extensions.md:104:| `trustProject` | The `trust_project` input |
docs/extensions.md:105:| `ui` | `{ ask, notify }`, the GitHub UI (see [Questions on GitHub](#questions-on-github)). Only in `comment` mode on an issue or pull request. Not set in `output` mode or for direct prompts |
docs/extensions.md:110:### `trust_project`
docs/extensions.md:112:`trust_project` (default `false`) tells the extension that it can load and run the configuration of the repository. For pit, this is `.pi/pit.json` and `.pi/functions`.
docs/extensions.md:114:Anyone who can push a branch or open a pull request can change those files. Set `trust_project: true` only for repositories whose code you already run. Do not set it in workflows that run on pull requests from people you do not trust.
docs/how-it-works.md:23:6. **Collect the requests** ([`src/triggers.ts`](../src/triggers.ts)). In `comment` mode, pi-action collects all `@pi` comments on the thread that have no answer, not only the comment of the event. The first request of a new thread gets the full context of the issue or pull request. Later requests are follow-ups. See [Prompts](prompts.md).
docs/how-it-works.md:54:| `▶` | A request that pi gets: who asked, where, and its first line. For a [prompt template](prompts.md#prompt-templates), the line as typed and where the template comes from | |
docs/prompts.md:29:1. The `pi.prompts` files and directories of each package in `extensions`, in the order of the input. This includes packages with a pi-durable extension.
docs/prompts.md:30:2. `.pi/prompts/*.md` in the repository, **only with `trust_project: true`**. See [Security](security.md#prompt-templates-from-the-repository).
docs/prompts.md:31:3. `<agent_dir>/prompts/*.md`, when `agent_dir` is set.
docs/prompts.md:47:- pi-action expands templates in the [task](#the-task) of the first message (also `{{task}}` in `prompt_template`), of each follow-up, and in `prompt` (for `pr_number` runs and direct prompts). It does not expand answers to questions.
docs/prompts.md:90:| `{{diff}}` | Diff of the pull request. Empty for issues and direct prompts | A unified diff |
docs/prompts.md:92:| `{{trigger_comment}}` | The full text that contains the trigger phrase, after pi-action removes HTML comments and invisible characters. The task, for `pr_number` runs and direct prompts | `@pi please review this code` |
docs/prompts.md:211:| A later comment does not use the template | This is correct. The template is only for the first message of a new thread. Later comments are [follow-ups](#prompts-and-templates) |
docs/security.md:75:- Keep `trust_project` off, unless you trust all people who can change the repository. See [Extensions](extensions.md#trust_project).
docs/security.md:79:A [prompt template](prompts.md#prompt-templates) becomes the request of the user. Anyone who can push a branch can change the files in `.pi/prompts`. Thus, pi-action loads them only with `trust_project: true`. Without it, pi-action writes `Not loading the prompt templates in .pi/prompts: trust_project is off` to the log. Templates from `extensions` and from `agent_dir` load in all cases.
docs/threads.md:109:- Direct prompts have no thread, so they have no snapshots.
docs/workflows.md:83:## Output mode and direct prompts
docs/workflows.md:139:- The diff and the description go into the first message of a new thread only. When the thread of the pull request exists, the run sends only the task as a [follow-up](prompts.md). pi can get the new diff with its tools.
README.md:99:| `trust_project` | Let pi-durable extensions load and run the configuration of the repository (see [Extensions](docs/extensions.md#trust_project)) | No | `false` |
README.md:100:| `agent_dir` | Agent directory (user-level state) for pi-durable extensions, relative to the workspace | No | (a new temporary directory in `RUNNER_TEMP`) |
README.md:105:| `prompt_template` | Template for the first message of a new thread (see [Prompts](docs/prompts.md#custom-templates)) | No | (built-in prompt) |
README.md:107:| `prompt` | Task for the agent. Without `pr_number`, it needs `output_mode: output` (see [Workflow recipes](docs/workflows.md#output-mode-and-direct-prompts)) | No | - |
README.md:134:| [Prompts and templates](docs/prompts.md) | What pi receives, and how to change it with `prompt_template` |

